Moment captures a personal timeline now and keeps it portable and searchable later.

Usage:
  moment [flags]
  moment [command]

Available Commands:
  backup      Export, inspect, and restore portable data
  comment     Inspect and manage comments
  dev         Build deterministic development scenarios
  doctor      Diagnose runtime and data health
  help        Help about any command
  init        Initialize the Moment instance and owner
  location    Resolve post locations
  media       Inspect and maintain managed media
  owner       Manage the single site owner
  post        Create and manage Moments
  search      Search and rebuild the memory index
  serve       Run the Moment HTTP server
  site        Inspect and update site identity
  version     Show build identity

Flags:
      --data-dir string     local Moment data directory (direct mode)
  -h, --help                help for moment
      --json                write one machine-readable JSON document to stdout
      --log-format string   stderr log format: text or json (default "text")
      --log-level string    stderr log level: error, warn, info, or debug (default "info")
      --no-input            fail instead of prompting for input
      --timeout duration    maximum command duration (default 30s)
      --token-file string   file containing the owner API token
      --url string          Moment HTTP API base URL (API mode)

Use "moment [command] --help" for more information about a command.
